From 58b16b4ac52ea7bf5f179730b40edaa738b3c923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:41:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] OpenGL ES 2 renderer (PC_GLES) for the Vita's vitaGL,
 testable on Linux

pc/gl_shaders_gles.h: the PS1 texture lookup (4/8-bit CLUT, 15-bit, texture
window) in float arithmetic on a LUMINANCE_ALPHA texture store, the kept weight
in alpha instead of dual-source blending, and depth from the vertex stage (a
projective depth, linear in clip space) instead of gl_FragDepth. The backend's
ES 2 differences are under PC_GLES: client-side vertex arrays, quad blits for
glBlitFramebuffer, row packing for UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH, RGBA readbacks, screens at
the PS1's resolution. THPS_GLES=1 builds it on Linux; against the 3.3 renderer
at THPS_GL_SCALE=1 the attract-mode frames match to 0.03% of pixels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwhU758snL1NnmSbmmwENz
